      "message": "fix(import): refuse a STEP face whose tessellation never converges\n\ntruck's surface subdivision recurses forever on a B-spline or NURBS face\nthat is not continuous (one seam stays \"far\" at every depth), inside a\nrayon task nothing can interrupt, and with no facet produced the facet\nbudget never fires: the import hung (#1536, a 62-face filleted cube ran\nfor 19 CPU-minutes).\n\nEvery face is now wrapped in a metered surface (step_guard). B-spline and\nNURBS faces are divided by truck's own generic parameter_division called\non the wrapper - the same algorithm, so the same mesh - and past\nFACE_EVAL_CAP evaluations in one pass the wrapper answers with a fixed\npoint (the subdivision stops within one sweep) and an empty division (no\nrunaway grid is triangulated). The import is then refused naming the\nface's STEP entity, index, kind and shell. No thread is spawned, nothing\noutlives the call.\n\nPinned by import_step_guard (a discontinuous B-spline face refused by\nname inside a hard time limit, at the default and a lowered cap; a smooth\nB-spline dome still imports at its volume; degenerate knot variants end\ncleanly) and step_guard's unit tests (division identical to truck's on a\nsmooth surface, bounded and tripped on a discontinuous one, no work left\nrunning after a refused pass).\n\nFixes #1536\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
